OL,3,GNEWSAI am now the boss of my pain - it
OL,4,Ano longer controls me
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor years Julie-Ann Walkden had relied
OL,7,Fon pills and injections to cope with
OL,8,Fchronic pain, but it was an
OL,9,Funderstanding of what was going on that
OL,10,Fhelped her get her life back.
OL,12,F"I didn't want to take strong
OL,13,Fmedication which made me feel ill, not
OL,14,Fin control and often so confused that I
OL,15,Ffelt I'd dementia," she said.
OL,17,FShe was among more than 100 patients
OL,18,Fwho have completed a pain
OL,19,Frehabilitation programme, using
OL,20,Fexercise, talking and psychological
OL,21,Ftherapies to help them understand the
OL,22,Fsource of their pain.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
